From 123e3d598b01decf28496f97dca32583e14e6f0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:56:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify malformed public WebSocket pin arguments

Preserve Info, the existing public SPKI-pin argument/hint text and false
return before TLS context creation or dialer publication. Explicit public
pin metadata avoids a generic raw ConfigValue field. Bounded copied-string
truncation remains visible; no pin parser, comparison, credential, protocol
selection or key behavior changes.

Add a public-API case installing/restoring a marker dialer. Malformed input
must return false without invoking/replacing it; a subsequent explicit
marker call proves it remains installed. Only INVALID_SOCKET is supplied,
with no TLS, real sockets or network I/O. The empty offer is unreachable
on this path and avoids a native protocol constant in the shared test.
Check the actual diagnostic's exact text, option, argument and Info level.

Shared eCash owner after SPKI pinning19f848fc9c7. Source lint/diff pass;
new native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Sealed381/current intake unchanged.
Existing credential-bearing debug sites remain separately reported.

